    {
        "content": "<p>subotac opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14027\">PR #14027</a> from <code>subotac:fix/atomic-wait-big-endian</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Fixes #13988.</p>\n<p>WebAssembly linear memory is little-endian, while the native atomic views used by shared memory follow host endianness. Convert the expected wait32 and wait64 values at that boundary so comparisons use the same byte<br>\n  representation on big-endian hosts.</p>\n<p>Add the issue's wait32/wait64 regression cases and exclude the test from the pooling configuration, which does not support shared memory.</p>\n<p>Tests:</p>\n<p>- <code>cargo test --test wast -- atomic_wait_endianness</code><br>\n  - <code>cargo test --test wast -- threads</code><br>\n  - <code>cargo fmt -p wasmtime -p wasmtime-test-util -- --check</code></p>\n</blockquote>",
